senses.gloss:
āhāra, m.
(1) some member of a shipʼs crew, mentioned with nāvika and others Av 〔i.200.5〕; 〔ii.61.9〕; evidently = āhāraka, q.v.; perhaps tower, cf. Pali Jāt. 〔iv.159.16〕 (nāvaṃ) āharitvā gāmato, apparently having towed away from the village; cf. also āharaṇa;
(2) in Mvy 〔798〕 = Tib. rgyud, usually = tantra; perhaps a mystic technique in general, or possibly bringing in in a more specific sense, see s.v. yamaka;
(3) district, province: Māy 〔28〕; see Hultzsch, Aśoka, 〔163 n. 11〕;
(4) āhāra, nt. = Skt. āhāra, m. food: Divy 〔13.7〕 ˚raṃ, n. sg.; same MSV 〔iii.22.10〕. On āhāra-kṛtya see s.v. kṛtya (2).
